<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="e7e90948-599a-526a-9d45-2869c2c67fda" activityNameId="756575db-5d2b-5d46-bb86-01f0764938e6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Barge</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Barge
The exchanges of the barge manufacturing are derived from an assessment of one barge, with a load capacity of 2800t. This data was adjusted to model a barge, representing the current average total capacity for solid goods transports (1000 tonnes/barge). Energy consumption in manufacturing was estimated as 50% of the cumulative energy of the used materials. The split of energies is 10% electricity and 90% heavy fuel oil.;
UUID: 789a5d04-1198-3e33-845d-14b3f6808fc9
This inventory calls processes of material production, representing the material composition of an average water vehicle used for solid goods transportation. For manufacturing, electricity and heavy oil burned in industrial furnace are included. For the transportation of materials standandard distance are applied. Also, waste treatment processes for non metal components of a water vehicle are accounted for.
Location: Manufacturing data represents conditions in Europe.
Technology: The modelled barge is considered as a mix for motorships and push tugs.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature studies and own calculations. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_789a5d04-1198-3e33-845d-14b3f6808fc9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
